---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/memorial.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="In Memoriam | AMD FFL">
<main class="memorial-page">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow">Forever part of the league</div>
      <h1>In Memoriam</h1>
      <p>Remembering the owners who helped make the AMD Fantasy Football League what it is.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell memorial">
    <section class="memorial-entry" aria-labelledby="terry-kennedy">
      <article class="tribute">
        <div class="portrait">
          <div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/images/memorial/terry.jpg" alt="Terry Kennedy" /></div>
          <div class="identity">
            <span>Original Owner</span>
            <h2 id="terry-kennedy">Terry Kennedy</h2>
            <strong>Cathedral Golden Gales</strong>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="story">
          <div class="eyebrow">The Glue. My Rival.</div>
          <p>Terry Kennedy was an original owner and 1 of the toughest competitors in this league. If he made it to the playoffs, he was going all the way. He made it to 8 Championship games in 16 1/2 seasons. Football was important to him. He often told family to not call during gametime, “I'm playing Fantasy Football.” He loved Canada and the animals that came to his yard. We had several conversations about the wildlife that visited him.</p>
          <p>For all of the conversations that we had, and the opinions he gave, he kept to himself. No wife or family close, he didn't share his health. He always let on that he was ok. He had several heart attacks and spent time in the hospital where we had no idea. He enlisted in the Canadian military when he was 17.</p>
          <p>Thank you for all the memories and everything that you brought and gave to this league. You are 1 of the reasons that this league has lasted this long. The glue. My rival. I called hospitals looking for you at the start. And now at the end.</p>
          <blockquote>You will always be part of this league as we will name the Championship after you. You had been there so many times over the years, it only makes sense.</blockquote>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="legacy" aria-label="Terry Kennedy league legacy">
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>4×</span><strong>League Champion</strong></div>
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>8</span><strong>Championship Appearances</strong></div>
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>11</span><strong>Postseason Appearances</strong></div>
      </div>

      <div class="cathedral">
        <small>His legacy lives on in</small>
        <h3>The Cathedral Bowl</h3>
        <p>The league championship carries Terry's team name forward every season.</p>
        <div class="memorial-signoff">Forever AMD FFL</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="memorial-entry" aria-labelledby="jake-calhoun">
      <article class="tribute">
        <div class="portrait">
          <div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/images/memorial/jake-calhoun.jpg" alt="Jake Calhoun" /></div>
          <div class="identity">
            <span>Original Owner</span>
            <h2 id="jake-calhoun">Jacob “Jake” Calhoun</h2>
            <strong>March 30, 1982 — February 17, 2025</strong>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="story">
          <div class="eyebrow">Truly an original.</div>
          <p>Jake Calhoun was an original owner and an original character. For 19 seasons, he was part of the fabric of the AMD FFL — 176 wins, 8 playoff games, 1 Championship, and many opinions. Jake was never short on those opinions, and the league was more interesting because he was willing to share them.</p>
          <p>Gaming was a huge part of Jake's life. Through it, he found friendship, competition, companionship, and a second family. He was loved and respected by the people who knew him there. The AMD FFL was another one of those places where competition became community, and Jake was part of it from the beginning.</p>
          <p>Nineteen seasons is more than a statistic. It is years of drafts, lineup decisions, trades, arguments, wins, losses, conversations, rivalries, and laughs. Jake helped shape the personality of this league simply by being himself. His Championship is in the record book, his 176 wins are in the standings, but the character he brought to the league is the part no spreadsheet can capture.</p>
          <p>Jake passed away on February 17, 2025, at only 42 years old. He left far too soon, but after nearly two decades in this league, his place in its history is permanent.</p>
          <blockquote>Truly an original. 19 seasons, 176 wins, a Championship, and many opinions. Forever part of the AMD FFL family.</blockquote>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="legacy" aria-label="Jake Calhoun league legacy">
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>19</span><strong>Seasons</strong></div>
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>176</span><strong>Wins</strong></div>
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>8</span><strong>Playoff Games</strong></div>
        <div class="legacy-item"><span>1×</span><strong>League Champion</strong></div>
      </div>

      <div class="memorial-signoff memorial-signoff--entry">Forever AMD FFL</div>
    </section>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
